# librocat, self-hosted: its settings (SELF_HOSTING.md). ./setup.sh copies
# this file to .env on its first run and adds the secrets at the end. After a
# change: docker compose up -d --build

# --- Models ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Your agent is the System Two. librocat's server uses one model, a System
# One, and writes nothing itself: the writing (descriptions, tags, merges)
# and the searching are your agents'. librocat Cloud runs Jev, and with Jev a
# self-hosted librocat works like Cloud. The model is optional: without it,
# cataloging and Libro's screens are off, search works the same (it goes by
# words), and your agents still read and write the library.
#   System One   typed judgments (yes or no, one of a set, a score): catalogs
#                a concept an agent left blank from its own sentences and your
#                tags, suggests review dates, confirms duplicates, and checks
#                your agents' merge drafts. Jev (TypeSafe, hosted), or an
#                open-source one you run offline, so nothing leaves this server.
# Check it with ./models.sh, and how well it does librocat's jobs with
# ./models.sh judge (SELF_HOSTING.md has the scores we measured).

# Jev through the Vercel AI Gateway, as on librocat Cloud:
# AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY=
# From TypeSafe (a key from https://console.typesafe.ai/keys):
# TYPESAFE_API_KEY=
# Your own, offline: docker compose --profile systemone up -d --build (Von, on
# the CPU), or any server that speaks TypeSafe's /v1/systemone (Kev or
# OpenJev on a GPU).
# LIBROCAT_JEV_URL=http://systemone:8000/v1
# LIBROCAT_JEV_KEY=
# The server's model, which the concepts it catalogs record (Von's: von-latest).
# LIBROCAT_EVAL_MODEL=von-latest
# local, gateway, typesafe, or off. Unset: the one that has settings (yours
# first, then TypeSafe's key, then the gateway's), else off.
# LIBROCAT_JEV=

# --- Email -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Sign-up and password codes through Resend. Unset, they go to the log
# (./logs.sh --history 100).
# AUTH_RESEND_KEY=

# --- Address -----------------------------------------------------------------
# LIBROCAT_PORT=3000
# Behind a domain, with a reverse proxy (SELF_HOSTING.md):
# LIBROCAT_SITE_URL=https://kb.example.com
# CONVEX_CLOUD_ORIGIN=https://convex.kb.example.com
# CONVEX_SITE_ORIGIN=https://auth.kb.example.com
# LIBROCAT_BIND=127.0.0.1
# 1 lets the reading list and source watch fetch pages on your own network:
# LIBROCAT_FETCH_PRIVATE=1

# --- Secrets -----------------------------------------------------------------
# ./setup.sh writes them below. Keep them: they are the key to your data.
